        "id": "ch21_5-2",
        "text": "404   PART 5 The Part of Tens\nThe only quirk is that different Linux distributions use different software package\nformats (as discussed in Chapter 15), and thus different command line tools. When\nyou use command line tools to install software, you need to know which format\nyour Linux distribution uses so you know which tool to use. The two basic package\nformats used in Linux are:\n\u00bb\n\u00bb  Debian Package Management: Used by Debian, Ubuntu, Mint, and other\nDebian-based Linux distributions\n\u00bb\n\u00bb  Red Hat Package Management: Used by Red Hat, CentOS, Fedora, open-\nSUSE, and other Red Hat-based Linux distributions\nIn this step, I cover both methods of installing the server software packages.\nBy using the distribution software packages for each server, you\u2019re guaranteed\nthat the server will run correctly in your Linux environment. An additional benefit\nis that as you update the distribution software, they will include any security\npatches or bug fixes releases for the Apache, MySQL, and PHP servers\nautomatically.\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Installing servers in Ubuntu\n\u2022 Installing servers in openSUSE\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
